  <main class="page" id="main">
    <section class="hero flow">
      <p class="card-note">Cafe · Identity and site · 2025</p>
      <h1>Fern &amp; Kettle</h1>
      <p class="lead">A one-page site with a menu the owners change themselves before opening each morning.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="prose flow">
      <h2>The brief</h2>
      <p>Fern &amp; Kettle opened with a chalkboard menu and a social media account that nobody had time to update. Customers kept asking whether the cafe did breakfast, which it did, and whether it took bookings, which it did too.</p>
      <h2>What we built</h2>
      <p>A single page with the opening hours at the top, the menu below, and a booking link that goes straight to the cafe's existing calendar. The menu prints cleanly on one sheet, so the counter copy and the website are always the same.</p>
      <h2>Since launch</h2>
      <p>The owners update the menu most mornings in a couple of minutes. Phone calls asking about opening hours have mostly stopped.</p>
      <p><a href="/#work">Back to all work</a></p>
    </section>
    <section class="section-contact">
      <h2>Need something similar?</h2>
      <p class="body">Tell us what your site needs to do and we will reply within a few days.</p>
      <p class="action"><a href="/about/#contact">Start a project</a></p>
    </section>
  </main>
  <footer class="site-footer">
